issioners and of course and  their staff for basically uh giving us  what we asked for  strict but fair  we thought this would apply to all other  member states but i think a moment of  humility is sometimes also in place it  was also applied to us as it should be  and it improved the end product and  ultimately if we can  transform if we innovate and if we can  manage the transition the experience of  the rrp will also really be one of  example that will enable the european  union to remain strong and even more  effective so thank you for that as well  another floor thank you so much  yeah thank you very much prime minister  dear mark uh deputy prime minister dear  sigrid thank you very much for having me  here  mayor thank you very much for having me  here in rotterdam  indeed um rotterdam is the home of  europe's biggest port biggest harbour  you said it is the heart of the dutch  economy well i would say as such with a  hard dutch economy it's also a  bellwether  for the health not only of the dutch  economy but also the european economy so  if the port is doing well our economy is  also doing well  and this port really is europe's gateway  for trade with the rest of the world  to be the gateway for trade with the  rest of the world you need the capacity  and you need to innovate and i know this  is very dear to your heart  so maratha dam is a model for both the  project we visited this afternoon  illustrates this perfectly i must say i  was fascinated to visit the alphanar  it's amazing to see that ship driven by  battery power  and demonstrating the zero emission  inland waterway project that has been  developed here  as we all know transport is one of um  the sectors where the carbon emissions  at the moment being are rising  um  going thus against the trend that we  have in all the other sectors that the  co2 emissions are decreasing so it's of  utmost importance that you innovate and  that we have solutions for example also  in the maritime transport and we