endency on  russian fossil fuels you know that we  have stopped the import of coal that we  are winding down  uh the import of russian oil  it's going to be tough  but we have created regional  groups to make sure that the gas flows  where it is needed  we have emergency plans  if you look at in the wider perspective  i'm deeply convinced that we will  prevail because this is not only  a war that russia has unleashed against  ukraine but this is a question whether  autocracies will prevail or democracy  will prevail and i'm deeply convinced  that we have the longer breath and on  the other hand  if you look our sanctions are more and  more biting and grinding into the  russian economy there's a very  interesting yale study i can only  recommend to look at it  that shows how deep the sanctions are  cutting and this is increasing week by  week that's the way we designed them  yes i know that for quite a long time  putin has been able to partially cushion  this  decrease  or the yeah of the  russian economy by revenues from fossil  fuels  and that's why it's so important that we  keep on track as i said the numbers are  telling that i just displayed yeah most  important of course is that most  important of course is that europe  remains solidare solidaria to one  another  do you trust that all countries will be  solidary yes i am convinced that this is  the case of course we always have to  discuss the details but  we have made a crucial experience  uh during the pandemic  at the very beginning there the member  states tried to go on their own  nationally  closing down borders export bans you  name it and then we realized this is too  big for each one of us  and then we stood together  and we  discovered the strength of sharing  and of solidarity  and as i said much much more than 27 we  are much stronger than 27 countries  together this is the european union  with all the power that is behind it and  if you look in hindsight this region  has gone pretty well through the  pandemic i'm very proud that we were the  only region worldwide that stayed open  for export of these life-saving vaccines  this has not been forgotten we take i  think we can take pride in that  and this experience of empowerment if we  stand together  this is still in our memory and now we  have the next crisis and it is a huge  crisis that we are going through  but if we stick together  with unity solidarity and determination  we will overcome  last question financial  thank you question for uh the prime  minister um yesterday and uh miss van  der lion uh put forward a proposal for  tackling the energy crisis and with one  of the most striking proposals being  putting a price cap on  energy prices and i was wondering what  the dutch position the division of the  dutch government is in that regard yes  that debate will take place tomorrow in  the energy council on celebrity  the state secretary will participate but  generally we are looking favorably at  the commission proposals of course we  have questions on particular proposals  and how to implement how to make sure  that there is enough flexibility  on implementation but generally we have  a favorable look at  the whole package  including  the idea  of  what they have done now in germany  in terms of  capping some of the prices and how could  we do that at the european level  we have again  taken a look at our position on a price  cap on  russian pipeline gas  we still have questions and worries but  we take a more positive view on those  proposals and again it will be debated  tomorrow and  then i get i think the commission will  reassess what comes out of the council  and um i hope the  the energy ministers can then as soon as  possible come to final conclusions  thank you very much  have a safe trip home  [Applause]
 

